saving a family after death three  urns all belonging to the same family  were found abandoned at a senior living  facility  two of the deceased are veterans after  someone suggested throwing them away a  community is coming together to make  sure they make it to their final resting  place with full military honors  victoria saha has the story you will  only see  for more than a year and a half the  remains of stella  her husband theodore and their son  ernest stayed abandoned at the clark  towers assisted living  after their other son who was holding  onto his family's ashes  died apartment manager tammy wilpe found  the urns tucked away in a closet for  decades  but quickly realized there was no other  family to hand them over to i would  never be able to throw them away  i couldn't not knowing what to do she  called reverend grace thompson for help  when i called los angeles because these  three are from los angeles  and the cremains were actually um  the bodies were actually processed in  los angeles they couldn't help me either  and i was told three times in los  angeles to throw them away  with a little bit of digging they found  out theodore and his son ernest were  veterans  i'm so honored to say i'm their  guardians  from the veterans cemetery which means  that  i'm responsible for them and i really  took that  seriously to make sure that my  three urns had a proper burial  but their mom stella was not going to be  allowed to be buried with them  unless someone paid a 450 dollar fee  we wanted them to be together they were  in life and they needed to be in death  so the veterans of foreign war groups  stepped in to help with the funds  it was a no-brainer for us  we did bring it up at our meeting on the  12th of june  and the entire post voted voted to do  that  the family of three urns will be laid to  rest together with full military honors  on july 13  at the veterans cemetery in boulder city  victoria saha  8 news now nice ending there  as for the apartment manager tammy wilpe  she told her residents to let her know  if they have urns  and who to give them to in the event of  their passing  additionally reverend thompson's church  came up with a program called from womb  to tomb that offers guidance on  abandoned urns
 

